# Search-Detect-Land - ArduCopter 4.6.3 parameter changes
# Supersedes fixes-2026-08-02.param. One value revised; see MOT_THST_HOVER.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS TWICE
# The 2026-08-02 set WAS written to the vehicle (logs/params.param is a live
# read at STAT_BOOTCNT=62 containing all of it), but the board came up on
# 2026-08-07 at boot 63 with every value reverted to stock. STAT_RUNTIME also
# went backwards, 31660 -> 31257, which a monotonic firmware-written counter
# cannot do unless the parameter storage rolled back. Log 82 therefore flew on
# stock gains and reproduced the oscillation unchanged (9.8 Hz, roll gyro std
# 20.9 deg/s vs 21.8 in log 80).
#
# => After writing these, POWER-CYCLE and read them back before flying.
#    If they revert again, the board's parameter storage is failing.

# --- 1. Hover throttle (REVISED 2026-08-07) ---
# Measured from log 82: CTUN.ThO = 0.147, sd 0.0022, over 573 samples with
# |climb rate| < 20 cm/s. Was 0.108 on 2026-08-02 - the airframe is heavier now
# and the pack was lower (22.85 V at arm vs 24.12 V). Stock 0.3297 puts the
# mixer's average-throttle floor (MOT_THST_HOVER * ATC_THR_MIX_MAX) at 0.165,
# ABOVE hover, which is what caused the uncommanded climb and the log 81 crash.
MOT_THST_HOVER,0.147                # was 0.3297; floor becomes 0.0735

# --- 2. Kill the 10 Hz oscillation ---
# Loop gain as-flown 0.99 (sustained limit cycle). These put it near 0.52.
# D was the dominant term at 10 Hz: 0.134 of the 0.198 output, vs 0.094 for P.
# Leave ATC_RAT_*_FLTD and *_FLTT at 20 - moving the gyro filter to 40 restores
# the intended FLTD = gyro_filter/2 relationship without editing them.
# INS_GYRO_FILTER was 20, a default meant for 12-inch-plus props. It costs
# 26.6 deg of phase lag at 10 Hz, versus 14.0 deg at 40 Hz.
INS_GYRO_FILTER,40
ATC_RAT_RLL_P,0.08                  # was 0.135
ATC_RAT_RLL_I,0.08                  # was 0.135 (kept equal to P by convention)
ATC_RAT_RLL_D,0.0015                # was 0.0036
ATC_RAT_PIT_P,0.08                  # was 0.135
ATC_RAT_PIT_I,0.08                  # was 0.135
ATC_RAT_PIT_D,0.0015                # was 0.0036
# Yaw: REVERTED TO STOCK 2026-08-07. These were halved as a precaution in the
# 08-02 set, which the data does not justify - yaw's controller output at 10 Hz
# measured 5 units against 6865 in the gyro, so yaw was not participating in the
# oscillation, and stock yaw gains were demonstrably not oscillating in logs 80
# and 82. Halving them only costs heading-hold authority. It also put both below
# their documented metadata range (ATC_RAT_YAW_P 0.180-0.60, ATC_RAT_YAW_I
# 0.01-0.06), which is what triggers Mission Planner's out-of-range warning.
# That warning is advisory - the firmware does not clamp these - but there is no
# reason to be outside the range here.
ATC_RAT_YAW_P,0.18                  # stock
ATC_RAT_YAW_I,0.018                 # stock

# --- 3. Battery protection (6S) ---
BATT_LOW_VOLT,21.0                  # was 10.5, a 3S value that could never fire
BATT_CRT_VOLT,19.8                  # was 0
BATT_FS_LOW_ACT,1                   # 1 = Land. RTL needs GPS, which isn't fitted.
BATT_FS_CRT_ACT,1

# --- 4. Radio failsafe margin ---
# TX sends 982 us at throttle-bottom; trip point was 975. 7 us is not margin.
# Also redo the RC calibration: RC1_MIN reads 1002 but the TX sends 982.
FS_THR_VALUE,950                    # was 975

# --- 5. No GPS is fitted; stop telling the EKF to expect one ---
# EKF altitude drifted up to 3.5 m from baro mid-flight. Log 82 still shows it:
# CTUN.Alt spans -4.55 to +2.09 m on a flight that never left ~1 m.
# Leave EK3_SRC1_POSZ = 1 (Baro) and EK3_SRC1_YAW = 1 (Compass) alone.
# When the AprilTag pose feed is live, POSXY/VELXY become 6 (ExternalNav).
EK3_SRC1_POSXY,0                    # was 3 (GPS)
EK3_SRC1_VELXY,0                    # was 3 (GPS)
EK3_SRC1_VELZ,0                     # was 3 (GPS)

# --- 6. Thrust/voltage compensation ---
# OPTIONAL ON FLIGHT 1. This changes the throttle->thrust mapping, so it shifts
# the effective hover point and confounds the tune measurement. If you want one
# variable at a time, skip these two until the oscillation is confirmed gone,
# then add them and let MOT_HOVER_LEARN=2 re-settle MOT_THST_HOVER in AltHold.
MOT_BAT_VOLT_MAX,25.2               # was 0 (compensation off)
MOT_BAT_VOLT_MIN,19.8               # was 0

# --- Verification, in this order ---
# 1. Write all of the above.
# 2. POWER-CYCLE the flight controller (not just a soft reboot).
# 3. Reconnect, Refresh Params, and confirm ATC_RAT_RLL_P reads 0.08 and
#    MOT_THST_HOVER reads 0.147. If either reverted, STOP - storage is failing.
# 4. Flight 1: Stabilize only, ~1 m, hover 30-60 s.
# 5. Pull the log and check:
#      - RATE.R  : is the 9.8 Hz peak gone or much smaller?
#      - RCOU    : are motors still hitting 1090?
#      - CTUN.ThO at steady hover -> confirms MOT_THST_HOVER.
# 6. Still oscillating? Halve D again. One change at a time.
# 7. Flight 2: AltHold, still low. Confirm it holds AND descends when asked.
# 8. Then AUTOTUNE, one axis at a time via AUTOTUNE_AXES.
#
# Keep LOG_BITMASK as-is - the fast attitude logging is what made this
# measurable. Consider LOG_DISARMED=1 to capture the boot window; log 82's
# "Arm: Gyros inconsistent" happened before logging opened, so it's invisible.
